{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"4043256d8ce6767d09a8896b7cfac7be1fd34f002eccdb48cb1186fec9ec38fa","digest":{"component_or_area":"grounding metric backend (Engine B)","key_entities":["src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke","src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_scc_files","rebar.builtin.smell.metric-oversize","src/rebar/metrics/analyzers/scc_loc.py","--by-file","--format json","Files array"],"problem_keywords":["scc command missing flag","per-file json","metric detection","threshold matching","grounding backend"],"propositions":["The grounding metric backend _metric_invoke invokes scc without the --by-file flag, causing scc to return empty Files arrays in language summaries instead of per-file entries.","The _scc_files function depends on Files array entries from scc JSON output but receives empty arrays, preventing the threshold loop from executing and blocking all metric matches.","With scc 3.7.0, the metric-oversize detector never emits documented over-800-LOC file matches because no per-file entries are available to evaluate against the cutoff.","The analogous code-health adapter already implements the correct --by-file flag (bug rapid-cuboid-velvetcrab), establishing the expected scc output contract for per-file consumers."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787887462569907001,"uuid":"0fdc5efd-8c09-48b5-933a-52898ca37ba5"}